# The number-field test matrix, defined once and included by every
# number-field test file (each file also runs standalone; re-inclusion just
# rebinds the same values — Oscar caches the fields):
#
#   K7  = Q(sqrt-7)        imaginary, h = 1, 2 split — KR's own example field
#   K2  = Q(sqrt2)         totally real, h = 1, 2 ramified — the Algorithm 4
#                          correction field
#   Kr5 = Q(sqrt5)         totally real, h = 1, 2 inert
#   K5  = Q(sqrt-5)        imaginary, h = 2 — the class group is generated by
#                          the dyadic prime, so 2C_S is forced trivial (the
#                          recorded Algorithm 1 divergence)
#   K21 = Q(sqrt-21)       imaginary, C = Z/2 x Z/2 — rank-2 2-torsion;
#                          the lambda_b branch fires
#   K34 = Q(sqrt34)        the anisotropic-dimension blind-spot witness field;
#                          also totally real with 2 ramified, h = 2, and the
#                          dyadic prime PRINCIPAL (6 + sqrt34 has norm 2) — the
#                          one field of the matrix where lambda_b coexists with
#                          real places
#   Kc  = Q[x]/(x^3-3x-1)  totally real cubic, three orderings
#   K32 = Q[x]/(x^3-2)     mixed signature, one real and one complex place
#   Ks10 = Q(sqrt10)       totally real, 2 ramified, h = 2. NOT a lambda_b
#                          field: the dyadic prime is non-principal and its
#                          class generates Cl, so 2-torsion of C_S vanishes for
#                          every admissible S (the same mechanism as K5) — the
#                          real-places-plus-lambda_b combination lives on K34
#                          instead. Here for the Algorithm 4 dyadic correction
#                          with h = 2 and for mixed sign patterns.
#   K162 = Q(zeta_16)^+    = Q[x]/(x^4-4x^2+2), totally real quartic, h = 1,
#                          2 TOTALLY RAMIFIED with e = 4: ord_P(4) = 8, so the
#                          corrected Algorithm 4 modulus exponent is >= 9 —
#                          wild dyadic ramification, the deepest prime-2 corner
#   K2i = Q(sqrt-2)        imaginary, 2 ramified, h = 1 — the non-real control
#                          isolating dyadic ramification from formal reality
#
# plus the totally real quartic Kq and KQ = rationals_as_number_field() used
# by specific suites. The stated field properties are not trusted: the
# "field matrix properties" testset in test_number_fields.jl asserts each one.

using Oscar

K7, s7 = quadratic_field(-7)
K2, s2 = quadratic_field(2)
Kr5, sr5 = quadratic_field(5)
K5, s5 = quadratic_field(-5)
K21, s21 = quadratic_field(-21)
K34, s34 = quadratic_field(34)
Qx, x = polynomial_ring(QQ, "x")
Kc, ac = number_field(x^3 - 3x - 1, "a")
K32, a32 = number_field(x^3 - 2, "b")
Kq, aq = number_field(x^4 - 4x^2 + 1, "c")
Ks10, s10 = quadratic_field(10)
K162, w16 = number_field(x^4 - 4x^2 + 2, "w")
K2i, s2i = quadratic_field(-2)
KQ, _ = Hecke.rationals_as_number_field()
